  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "* Moved ``DotExtensions.MsExtensions.StringSegments`` namespace to ``DotExtensions.MsExtensions.Primitives``\n* Moved ``DotExtensions.MsExtensions.StringValuePlural`` namespace to ``DotExtensions.MsExtensions.Primitives``\n* Merged DotExtensions.MsExtensions code into DotExtensions main package\n* Removed code deprecated for removal in v10\n* Removed dependency on DotPrimitives\n* Replaced deprecated DateTime ``DaysInYear`` static extension method with non static extension method\n* Renamed ``DayOfWeekInt`` extension method to ``CalculateDayOfWeekAsInteger``\n* Changed ``WeekOfMonth`` extension method to be an extension property\n* Renamed ``DaysInYear`` extension method to ``CalculateNumberOfDaysInYear``\n* Optimisations and performance improvements\n* Moved more exception messages to Resources resx file\n* Reworked GetRandomDrive static extension method to add optional parameter\n* Improves robustness of string and StringSegment Capitalization extensions\n* Added some missing xml doc comments\n* Improved helpfulness of some thrown exceptions\n* Renamed Windows based file permission extension methods for extra clarity\n* Reorganized Unix file permissions code into consolidated classes\n* Improved performance of Unix Permission Notation detection\n* Updated xml doc comments to use <see langword=true> and <see langword=false> instead of <c>true</c> or <c>false</c>\n* Moved file size labels to Resources resx file\n* Moved Safe File Enumeration code and namespace\n* Added ``GetNonNullPathRoot(string)`` and ``GetNonNullPathRoot(string?)`` static extension methods to Path - These method guarantees they will not return a null value.",
